# Fresh install, then every reachable onboarding step to Home with each step's real
# CTA. Longer than ~25 steps by necessity: a dozen-plus onboarding states, each
# proved with a wait + shot, plus the taps a choice screen needs before its CTA
# enables.
#
# Welcome (ProtectionPlanWelcomeView) hands off straight to painPoints.
#
# `trialGranted` is also skipped on purpose: OnboardingFlow.visibleStep migrates it
# to `.appBlocking` unconditionally (OnboardingFlow.swift:316-326), so ContentView's
# `.trialGranted` switch case can never run — not on the real reminderPlan -> next
# transition, and not even through its own debug deep link (see
# features/onboarding.md Gotchas). reminderPlan's real CTA already lands on
# appBlocking directly.
#
# appBlocking is the rehearsal (BlockingRehearsalView). Nobody touches it here,
# so each beat plays itself: this is the self-play pass on a real fresh install.
# Its picks need FamilyControls tokens, which the simulator cannot hand out, so
# they are reached via the `plus-app-blocking-setup?selected=` QA seam, then that
# screen's real "Continue" CTA.

fresh
launch
sleep 2  # the welcome CTA ignores taps while the splash fades

# welcome — ProtectionPlanWelcomeView. protectionPlanPrimaryCTA "Get started".
# ProtectionPlanScaffold.swift:219; content.primaryCTA = global.action.get_started.
wait id protectionPlanPrimaryCTA
shot welcome
tap --id protectionPlanPrimaryCTA

# painPoints — ProtectionPlanDistractionChoicesView. Needs one distraction choice
# AND one desired outcome before primaryCTA enables (canContinue,
# ProtectionPlanOnboarding.swift:30-31). Title: onboarding.personalise.pain.title.
# Chip labels: onboarding.personalise.choice.tiktok ("TikTok"),
# onboarding.personalise.outcome.simple ("A simpler routine").
wait text "What’s in the way?"
shot pain-points
tap --label TikTok
tap --label "A simpler routine"
tap --id protectionPlanPrimaryCTA

# missFrequency — ProtectionPlanFailureFrequencyView. Needs one frequency AND one
# risk window before primaryCTA enables (canContinue, ProtectionPlanOnboarding.swift
# :60-61). Title: onboarding.frequency.title. Labels: onboarding.frequency.rarely
# .title ("Rarely"), onboarding.risk_window.right_after ("Right after the reminder").
wait text "How often do you miss your pill?"
shot miss-frequency
tap --label Rarely
tap --label "Right after the reminder"
tap --id protectionPlanPrimaryCTA

# acquisitionSource — ProtectionPlanAcquisitionSourceView. Row id pattern
# acquisitionSource.<rawValue> (ProtectionPlanAcquisitionSourceView.swift:68).
# Title: onboarding.acquisition.title.
wait text "Where did you find Pillie?"
shot acquisition-source
tap --id acquisitionSource.tiktok
tap --id protectionPlanPrimaryCTA

# method — ProtectionPlanRoutineMethodView. Defaults to .pill, isPrimaryEnabled
# is always true (ProtectionPlanRoutineMethodView.swift:39), so no row tap needed.
# Title: onboarding.method.title.
wait text "Pick your method."
shot method
tap --id protectionPlanPrimaryCTA

# schedule, pill path — TodayPillView (ENG-138). Sealed pack, CTA disabled until a
# pill is tapped and answered. packTile.<n> ids come from PackCard's onSelectDay;
# todayPillQuestion / todayPillYes / todayPillLogged from TodayPillView. Title:
# onboarding.today_pill.title. Patch and ring get RoutineDialView (onboarding-dial.flow).
wait text "Tap the pill you’re on today."
shot today-pill
tap --id packTile.12
wait id todayPillQuestion
shot today-pill-tapped
tap --id todayPillYes
wait id todayPillLogged
shot today-pill-taken
tap --id protectionPlanPrimaryCTA

# reminderTime — ProtectionPlanReminderTimeView. Title: onboarding.reminder_time
# .title. CTA "Continue to notification settings" requests real notification
# authorization (OnboardingReminderCommit.swift; ProtectionPlanReminderTimeView
# .swift:178-187) — a real iOS system alert follows, unlike the FamilyControls
# request later, which is simulator-auto-approved. Confirm the button text live.
wait text "Pick a time."
tap --label Evening
wait text "Pill 12 · taken"
shot reminder-time
tap --id protectionPlanPrimaryCTA
tap --label Allow  # UNVERIFIED: iOS system notification-permission alert, not Pillie copy

# reminderPlan — ProtectionPlanDiagnosisView. The CTA is held back until the
# analyze-then-reveal beat finishes (ProtectionPlanDiagnosisView.swift:100-119),
# so wait on the id with a longer timeout, not the title (present during the
# analyzing beat too). Its real CTA lands directly on appBlocking
# (OnboardingFlow.nextStep(after: .reminderPlan), OnboardingFlow.swift:221-250) —
# trialGranted is not in between; see the header comment.
wait id protectionPlanPrimaryCTA 15
shot reminder-plan
tap --id protectionPlanPrimaryCTA

# appBlocking, beat 1: the reminder lands on the mini Home Screen. After 3.5 s
# untouched the demo taps the featured app (TikTok, the distraction picked above).
wait id blockingRehearsalBanner 15
sleep 1  # the banner drops in 0.6 s after the beat opens
shot rehearsal-reminder

# Beat 2: the app is paused. After 3 s the demo presses "Open Pillie".
wait id blockingRehearsalOpenPillie 10
shot rehearsal-paused

# Beat 3: the coral shake cover. After 4 s the clip plays through on its own.
wait id blockingRehearsalTapInstead 10
shot rehearsal-shake

# The ask, with the trial line of a fresh reverse trial. The simulator reports
# Screen Time as already allowed, so this is the ask after Allow: no Apple line,
# and "Use reminders only" is offered. onboarding-blocking-stages shoots the
# first-time ask.
wait id blockingRehearsalCheckedInPill 15
expect id appBlockingTrialLine
expect id blockingRehearsalRemindersOnly
sleep 1
shot rehearsal-ask

# The picks: sample tiles stand in for a FamilyControls selection, then the
# screen's real "Continue".
openurl "pillie://debug/plus-app-blocking-setup?selected=3&lang=en"
wait id blockingRehearsalChangePicks 15
shot rehearsal-picks
tap --id blockingRehearsalPrimary

# protectionPlanReady — ProtectionPlanReadyView. protectionPlanReadyStartButton
# (ProtectionPlanReadyView.swift:217), label "Go to Today" (onboarding.ready.cta).
wait id protectionPlanReadyStartButton
shot protection-plan-ready
tap --id protectionPlanReadyStartButton

# Home — pill 12 logged from the step 7 answer, streak 1.
wait text "Pill 12 of 28" 15
shot home
